{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2543","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2543","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2543\",\"parent_revision\":\"312f120f329501c3ba5055c0a3642e382d1a111a3e2b306146e2a6b9bb17b8ac\",\"root_revision\":\"312f120f329501c3ba5055c0a3642e382d1a111a3e2b306146e2a6b9bb17b8ac\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAfter a SAM task plan is created in `dh:add-new-feature` Phase 4, linking that plan to the backlog item is a separate follow-up call (`backlog_update(plan=...)`), distinct from plan creation itself. Because the link is a separable step, it can be omitted, folded into a subagent delegation prompt, or skipped on a subagent's self-report \u2014 and when that happens it fails silently, leaving the backlog item's `plan_path` null.\\n\\nWhere observed: issue #2510 reports `plan_path` null after Phase 4 (plan P3e7e163d for issue #2498, 2026-05-30). Downstream impact: `work-backlog-item` reads `plan_path` to route directly to `implement-feature`; a null value silently breaks that handoff and requires manual repair.\\n\\nRelationship to existing work: #2510 and PR #2542 address the *instruction* (reframing the Phase 4 step so it is reader-anchored and verified by post-condition). This item targets the deeper structural cause \u2014 that the link is a separate step at all \u2014 which the prose fix mitigates but does not eliminate. This is a distinct scope, not a duplicate of #2510.\\n\\nVerified structural facts (static read, 2026-06-03): `sam_plan create` stores plan YAML as a Gist artifact + plan-index entry but does not set the backlog item's plan field (`sam_schema/core/gist_task_layer.py`); the field is written only by `backlog_update(plan=...)` in `backlog_core/operations.py:719`; the value surfaces via `backlog_view(summary=True)` as `plan_path` (`backlog_core/server.py:1869,1881`).\\n\\n**User-provided context** (candidate direction for grooming/planning \u2014 not a requirement): make the plan link atomic with `sam_plan create` so no separate step exists, making the unlinked state unrepresentable. Open questions for grooming: the SAM server and `backlog_core` are separate MCP servers (create currently uses only the artifact-registry client, not backlog operations), so this couples two write paths; and the `issue=None` local-only plan case has no GitHub anchor for a plan comment, so any such change cannot be unconditional.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAll claims sourced from static reads of the repository on 2026-06-03:\\n\\n- `sam_plan create` does not call backlog operations: VERIFIED via `gist_task_layer.py` \u2014 `create_plan` calls `self._artifact_client.store()` and `self._plan_index.register()`; no import or call to `backlog_core` modules present.\\n- `_apply_plan_to_item` at `operations.py:719` is the exclusive `plan_path` writer: VERIFIED by grep across `backlog_core/` \u2014 only this function calls `update_item_metadata` with `{\\\"metadata\\\": {\\\"plan\\\": plan}}`.\\n- `plan_path` parsed by regex at `server.py:1869`: VERIFIED by reading `_build_summary_response` \u2014 `re.search(r\\\"^[Pp]lan:\\\\\\\\s*(\\\\\\\\S+)\\\", result.body, re.MULTILINE)`.\\n- Phase 4 verification block in `add-new-feature` SKILL.md: VERIFIED at lines 465-484 \u2014 read-verify-write pattern present.\\n- Issue #2510 closed, PR #2542 merged: VERIFIED via `backlog_view(selector='#2510', summary=True)` \u2014 status: closed.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-06-03)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n5/10 \u2014 Structural cause of a known data-integrity failure class. PR #2542 mitigates the most common trigger but does not prevent recurrence if a future orchestrator re-introduces the delegated-link anti-pattern. P2 because the mitigation exists; the structural fix removes the residual risk permanently.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Autonomous `work-backlog-item` routing from groomed to implement-feature. When `plan_path` is null, the skill cannot distinguish a freshly groomed item from one already planned, so it re-enters the planning pipeline unnecessarily or stalls pending manual repair.\\n- Bottleneck: Any session that relies on `work-backlog-item` to resume work after `add-new-feature` completes. A null `plan_path` turns a one-step resumption into a debug-and-repair task.\\n- Surface area: Any future orchestrator or skill that calls `sam_plan create` and assumes the backlog item will self-link is silently wrong by design.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Removes the entire null-`plan_path` failure class from the backlog lifecycle instead of mitigating it case-by-case.\\n- Makes the unlinked state either unrepresentable (atomic-coupling direction) or immediately detectable at the call site (enforcement direction).\\n- Enables `work-backlog-item` Step 4.3 to unconditionally trust `plan_path` as a routing signal without requiring defensive slug-search fallbacks.\\n- Reduces manual repair burden for operators who encounter a null `plan_path` after a planning session.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nAfter any workflow that creates a SAM plan for a backlog item completes successfully, `backlog_view(selector='#{issue}', summary=True)` returns a non-null `plan_path` matching the created plan's address. The unlinked state (`plan_path: null` with a plan in SAM storage) is either structurally unrepresentable or immediately surfaced as a tool-call error \u2014 not silently deferred to a downstream consumer.\\n\\nThree candidate directions (not a grooming requirement to select one \u2014 that is a planning decision):\\n\\n1. Atomic coupling: `sam_plan(action='create', issue=N)` calls `backlog_update(plan=...)` internally before returning. Cross-server write; requires either a shared backlog client inside the SAM server or a callback hook. The `issue=None` local-only case must remain unaffected.\\n\\n2. Post-condition enforcement: The Phase 4 verification block in `add-new-feature` is promoted from advisory prose to a hard gate. If `plan_path` is still null after the initial write attempt, the orchestrator retries the link (not the plan creation) and fails explicitly if the link cannot be written.\\n\\n3. Idempotent link-on-read: `backlog_view(summary=True)` detects `plan_path: null` and a matching SAM plan for the issue, then writes the link lazily. Minimal change; heals the unlinked state at read time rather than preventing it.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nA SAM plan creation workflow that, for any plan created with an associated GitHub issue, guarantees `backlog_update(plan=...)` is called and confirmed before the creation workflow signals completion. The guarantee must survive future skill edits, subagent delegation refactors, and new orchestrators invoking `sam_plan create` directly \u2014 not just the current `add-new-feature` Phase 4 prose.\\n\\nObservable target state: `backlog_view(selector='#{issue}', summary=True).plan_path` is non-null immediately after any successful `sam_plan create` call that includes an `issue` parameter.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. After `dh:add-new-feature` completes Phase 4 for an issue-linked backlog item, `backlog_view(selector='#{issue}', summary=True).plan_path` is non-null. Verify by calling `backlog_view` immediately after `sam_plan create` returns.\\n2. If `backlog_update(plan=...)` is not called (simulated by a test stub that skips the call), the system surfaces an explicit error or writes the link by another mechanism \u2014 `plan_path` is never null-and-silent.\\n3. For a plan created with `issue=None` (local-only, no GitHub anchor), no `backlog_update` call is attempted and no error is produced \u2014 the local-only path is unaffected by the change.\\n4. `work-backlog-item` invoked on an issue where Phase 4 just completed routes directly to `implement-feature` without re-entering the planning pipeline, confirming `plan_path` is correctly populated.\\n5. The fix does not require manual repair steps \u2014 no operator intervention is needed to restore `plan_path` after a normal `add-new-feature` run.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /dh:add-new-feature \u2014 Phase 4, lines 423-495 (plan creation and link step) |\\n| Skill | /dh:work-backlog-item \u2014 references/workflows/work/plan.md Step 4.3 (slug-search fallback) |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/gist_task_layer.py \u2014 `create_plan` (no backlog write path) |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py:719 \u2014 `_apply_plan_to_item` (exclusive plan_path writer) |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:1869 \u2014 `plan_path` regex parse in `backlog_view(summary=True)` |\\n| Backlog | #2510 \u2014 original bug report; closed; PR #2542 fixed instruction framing |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: #2542 (merged \u2014 mitigating instruction fix landed; this item targets the remaining structural gap)\\n- Blocks: None directly. Items relying on reliable `plan_path` routing in `work-backlog-item` benefit indirectly.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 Structural cause is fully understood; implementation scope depends on the chosen direction. Atomic coupling requires cross-server design work and test coverage for the conditional `issue=None` path. Post-condition enforcement is narrower but requires identifying the correct enforcement point (test, invariant, tool-level gate). Either direction requires regression tests covering the null-`plan_path` scenario.\\n\\n### Artifact Classification\\n\\n- Primary artifact type: Refactor\\n- Behavioral boundary: `plan_path` field in `backlog_view(summary=True)` after `sam_plan create` completes.\\n- Evaluation target: No execution path leaves `plan_path` null without an explicit error.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- Chosen refactor direction not decided. Three candidates exist (atomic coupling, post-condition enforcement, idempotent link-on-read). Planning requires one to be selected.\\n- Atomic-coupling direction requires design validation: can `GistTaskLayer.create_plan` call backlog operations without introducing a circular dependency between `plugin:dh:sam` and `plugin:dh:backlog`?\\n- For any direction touching `GistTaskLayer.create_plan`: confirm whether the `issue=None` (local-only plan) case requires conditional gating or is naturally excluded.\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n**Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface):**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/gist_task_layer.py` \u2014 `create_plan` method (atomic-coupling direction would add a backlog write here)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` \u2014 `_apply_plan_to_item` (enforcement or idempotent-read directions may add retry/detection logic here)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 `backlog_update` handler (no change expected) and `_build_summary_response` (idempotent-read direction would add lazy-link logic here)\\n\\n**Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface):**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 Phase 4 step (may become simpler or receive tighter gate wording)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/plan.md` \u2014 Step 4.3 slug-search fallback (may become redundant or validated by the fix)\\n\\n**Tests:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` \u2014 `test_backlog_update_success_with_plan` (line 1304)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_backlog/test_backlog_update_artifact_registration.py` \u2014 artifact registration on plan link\\n- New regression test needed: verify `plan_path` is non-null after `sam_plan create` with an issue number\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n- Issue #2510 (closed): documents the exact failure. Plan P3e7e163d created for issue #2498 on 2026-05-30; `plan_path` null in `backlog_view(summary=True)` response.\\n- Source evidence: `sam_schema/core/gist_task_layer.py` \u2014 `create_plan` uses `ArtifactRegistryClient.store()` only; no call to `backlog_update` or any backlog operations module.\\n- Source evidence: `backlog_core/operations.py:719` \u2014 `_apply_plan_to_item` is the only function that writes `metadata.plan` to a backlog item file and posts the GitHub Issue comment.\\n- Source evidence: `backlog_core/server.py:1869` \u2014 `plan_path` in `backlog_view(summary=True)` is parsed by `re.search(r\\\"^[Pp]lan:\\\\s*(\\\\S+)\\\", result.body, re.MULTILINE)` \u2014 a null plan means that pattern has no match in the issue body.\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n- Which candidate direction should planning target: (1) atomic coupling inside `sam_plan create`, (2) hard-gate post-condition enforcement in `add-new-feature` Phase 4, or (3) idempotent link-on-read in `backlog_view`?\\n- For the atomic-coupling direction: is a cross-server call from `plugin:dh:sam` to `plugin:dh:backlog` acceptable, or should the link be established through a shared client library instead?\\n- Should the enforcement also cover `work-backlog-item` Step 4.3 (which has its own slug-search fallback) or is that path already sufficient?\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n- Goal: Eliminate the silent-failure class where `backlog_update(plan=...)` is skipped after `sam_plan create`, leaving `plan_path` null.\\n- Status: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS\\n- AVAILABLE:\\n  - Structural root cause verified from source: `sam_plan create` (`gist_task_layer.py`) does not write to the backlog item's plan field; `backlog_update(plan=...)` in `operations.py:719` is the exclusive writer.\\n  - Observable failure instance documented: issue #2510, plan P3e7e163d for issue #2498, `plan_path` null after Phase 4, 2026-05-30.\\n  - `plan_path` read path confirmed: `backlog_view(summary=True)` parses a `Plan:` regex from the GitHub Issue body (`server.py:1869,1881`).\\n  - Current mitigating instruction in `add-new-feature` SKILL.md Phase 4 (lines 465-484): post-condition verification via read-verify-write cycle.\\n  - `work-backlog-item` Step 4.3 has its own slug-based search-and-link fallback (`plan.md` lines 33-66).\\n  - The two MCP servers (`plugin:dh:sam` and `plugin:dh:backlog`) are distinct processes; `GistTaskLayer.create_plan` uses only `ArtifactRegistryClient`, not backlog operations.\\n- DERIVABLE:\\n  - Failure probability from the structural gap: derivable from (a) the link step is orchestrator-owned, (b) it can be skipped when folded into a subagent delegation prompt, (c) `swarm-task-planner` self-reports are not evidence. All three confirmed by Phase 4 SKILL.md and the #2510 incident.\\n  - Impact on `work-backlog-item` routing: derivable \u2014 `plan_path` null means the item re-enters the full add-new-feature pipeline instead of routing directly to `implement-feature`.\\n- MISSING:\\n  - Chosen refactor direction not decided: three candidates exist (atomic coupling, post-condition enforcement, idempotent link-on-read). Planning cannot begin without a selection.\\n  - For atomic-coupling direction: whether `GistTaskLayer.create_plan` can call a backlog operation without circular dependency between the two MCP servers requires design validation.\\n  - For post-condition enforcement direction: the enforcement mechanism (test, invariant, linter, hook) is unspecified.\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. Create a backlog item with a linked GitHub Issue.\\n2. Invoke `dh:add-new-feature` for that item (or have `swarm-task-planner` create a plan and delegate the `backlog_update(plan=...)` call into the delegation prompt rather than keeping it in the orchestrator).\\n3. After the plan is created, call `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_view(selector='#{issue}', summary=True)`.\\n4. Observe `plan_path: null` in the response \u2014 the plan exists in SAM plan storage but the backlog item has no record of it.\\n5. Downstream: call `dh:work-backlog-item #{issue}` \u2014 the skill re-enters the full planning pipeline instead of routing to `implement-feature`.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **add-new-feature plan link is a separate skippable step after plan creation \u2014 silent-failure class** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation 2026-06-03 \u2014 analysis while reviewing PR #2536 / #2510\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-06-03\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"854a1026f26fa24211c0527269368fc2ab823f214ae7b988452267940ba4a591\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTA6cA\"}"}